Assistant: Now I can see that we need to wrap the ConfirmationContent with a Dialog component. Let's modify the preview file:

<file path=".temp/dessn-component-routes/ConfirmationContent-3d36f80f.tsx">
<change>
<description>Wrap ConfirmationContent with Dialog component and add necessary imports</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { Dialog } from '../../../../packages/ui/components/dialog/Dialog';
import { ConfirmationContent } from '../../../../packages/ui/components/dialog/ConfirmationDialogContent';

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    title: {
      type: "string",
      value: "Confirm Action",
      label: "Title",
    },
    variety: {
      type: "dropdown",
      value: "danger",
      options: ["danger", "warning", "success"],
      label: "Variety",
    },
    confirmBtnText: {
      type: "string",
      value: "Confirm",
      label: "Confirm Button Text",
    },
    cancelBtnText: {
      type: "string",
      value: "Cancel",
      label: "Cancel Button Text",
    },
    loadingText: {
      type: "string",
      value: "Loading...",
      label: "Loading Text",
    },
    isPending: {
      type: "boolean",
      value: false,
      label: "Is Pending",
    },
  });

  return (
    <Dialog defaultOpen={true}>
      <ConfirmationContent
        title={state.title.value}
        variety={state.variety.value as "danger" | "warning" | "success"}
        confirmBtnText={state.confirmBtnText.value}
        cancelBtnText={state.cancelBtnText.value}
        loadingText={state.loadingText.value}
        isPending={state.isPending.value}
        onConfirm={() => console.log("Confirmed")}
      >
        This is the content of the confirmation dialog. Are you sure you want to proceed?
      </ConfirmationContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:
1. Added import for the Dialog component
2. Wrapped the ConfirmationContent with Dialog component
3. Added defaultOpen={true} to ensure the Dialog is visible in the preview
4. Kept all the existing props and functionality

This should resolve the errors because now all the Dialog-related components (DialogClose, DialogTitle, and DialogDescription) will have access to the Dialog context they require.

